# F10 test: extruder sections without any heating hardware.
#
# A syringe extruder must be usable without declaring heater or sensor
# pins: the printer starts, M105 answers, G1 E moves and extruder homing
# all work, and the zero-temperature heater status both keeps the usual
# status keys and registers no heater or sensor.  With a heater-less
# extruder, a temperature request for zero is a no-op - only a request for
# a positive temperature is an error (see extruder_no_heater_error.test),
# so the no-op requests are exercised here.
DICTIONARY atmega2560.dict
CONFIG extruder_no_heater.cfg

# M105 works even though no heater or sensor is registered at all.
M105

# Heating commands for zero are accepted and do nothing.
M104 S0
M109 S0
TURN_OFF_HEATERS
M105

# The extruder status must look like a real heater's, with zero values.
ASSERT_HEATERLESS_EXTRUDER_STATUS

# The extruder steppers still home and move (F5 behaviour kept intact).
G28
G1 E10 F100
HOME_EXTRUDER EXTRUDER=extruder1
ACTIVATE_EXTRUDER EXTRUDER=extruder1
HOME_ACTIVE_EXTRUDER
G1 E45 F100
GET_POSITION
M114
M84
